<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tanzania People's Defence Force</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1964">1964</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as TPDF</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tanzania <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-defence-force">People's Defence Force</a> is the armed forces of Tanzania, created in 1964 after the mutiny of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanganyika-rifles">Tanganyika Rifles</a> to replace the old colonial-style army with a force loyal to the ruling party. It supported liberation movements in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idi-amin">Idi Amin</a>'s Uganda in the war of 1978 and 1979, and has served in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> peacekeeping, notably in eastern Congo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tanzania-peoples-defence-force.jpg" alt="Tanzania People's Defence Force" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: vectored by FOX 52 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tanzania_People%E2%80%99s_Defence_Force.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
